\title{Subspace (Relative) Topology}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{(X,\tau)} be a [topological space](def-000C) and let
    #{A\subseteq X}. The topology
    ##{
        \tau_A=\{A\cap U\mid U\in\tau\}
    }
    on #{A} is the \strong{subspace topology}, also called the
    \strong{relative topology}, induced by #{X}. Thus a subset of #{A} may be
    open in the subspace even when it is not open as a subset of #{X}.
}
